# See docs.aquasec.com/trivy > misconfiguration > ignore for syntax.
# Each entry below is a reviewed false positive / scan-harness artifact, not
# an accepted real risk -- see the comment above each ID.

# ConfigMap "secrets"/"sensitive content": neither finding is real secret
# material. AVD-KSV-0109 fires on both the literal `password`/`secret_key_base`
# System.get_env() *references* in configmap-akkoma.yaml (env var names, not
# values -- the real secret material lives in Kubernetes Secrets, injected
# via secretKeyRef in deployment.yaml) and independently on the ConfigMap
# data key's filename, `prod.secret.exs`, which matches on the word "secret"
# regardless of content. AVD-KSV-01010 fires on `email`/`notify_email`
# (rendered from .Values.akkoma.adminEmail -- a public admin contact
# address, not sensitive) and `username` (another System.get_env()
# reference). None of these are values that belong in a Kubernetes Secret.
AVD-KSV-0109
AVD-KSV-01010

# "Workloads in the default namespace": scan-harness artifact. CI's
# `helm template`/Trivy's own chart rendering doesn't pass a namespace, so
# rendered manifests default to "default". Real deployments (see
# argo-fleet's apps/akkoma/env/*/release.yaml) always target
# akkoma-{dev,staging,prod}, never the default namespace.
AVD-KSV-0110

# "CPU not limited": the akkoma container deliberately has no CPU limit --
# see values.yaml's resources block comment. The BEAM VM scheduler needs to
# see and use all available cores for efficient scheduling; a CPU limit
# would throttle it in ways that hurt latency more than an OOM-protected
# memory limit alone. Every other container in this chart (postgres, all
# init containers) does have a real CPU limit; this is the sole deliberate
# exception.
#
# CAVEAT: .trivyignore matches by rule ID only, not per-container -- if a
# future container is ever added without a CPU limit for a non-deliberate
# reason, this suppression will silently hide that finding too. Audit any
# new container's resources block manually; don't rely on this scan to
# catch it.
AVD-KSV-0011
